# `optim::presets::robust_internal_protocol`

The interior preset with larger budgets for difficult problems.

## Signature

```cpp
optim::OptimaOptions optim::presets::robust_internal_protocol();
```

## What It Does

Starts from [`presets::internal_protocol`](presets_internal_protocol.md) and raises the budgets: 160 iterations, longer line searches, more restoration and stall allowances, a larger nonmonotone window and trust-region cap, and two second-order-correction attempts. Use it when the plain interior preset runs out of iterations or stalls.

## Returns

An `OptimaOptions` ready to pass to `optima`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

Using the preset. It returns an ordinary `OptimaOptions`; the algorithm is `InternalProtocol`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  const optim::OptimaOptions options = optim::presets::robust_internal_protocol();
  out.writeln("algorithm =", optim::optima_algorithm_name(options.algorithm));
  const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc);
  out.writeln("x =", result.params.at("x").items<double>());
  out.writeln("exit =", optim::optima_exit_flag_name(result.exit_flag), ", iterations =", result.iteration, ", evaluations =", result.function_evaluations);
}
```

### Example 2

Adjusting a preset. A preset is a starting point: change any field afterwards.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  optim::OptimaOptions options = optim::presets::robust_internal_protocol();
  options.internal_protocol.max_iterations = 3;
  const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc);
  out.writeln("exit =", optim::optima_exit_flag_name(result.exit_flag), ", iterations =", result.iteration, ", evaluations =", result.function_evaluations);
}
```

### Example 3

What the preset changes: its values next to the defaults of the same algorithm.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <iostream>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const optim::OptimaOptions preset = optim::presets::robust_internal_protocol();
  optim::OptimaOptions plain;
  plain.algorithm = preset.algorithm;
  std::cout << "max_iterations = preset " << preset.internal_protocol.max_iterations << ", default " << plain.internal_protocol.max_iterations << "\n";
  std::cout << "max_line_search_iterations = preset " << preset.internal_protocol.max_line_search_iterations << ", default " << plain.internal_protocol.max_line_search_iterations << "\n";
  std::cout << "soc_correction_attempts = preset " << preset.internal_protocol.soc_correction_attempts << ", default " << plain.internal_protocol.soc_correction_attempts << "\n";
}
```

